From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] plat: ecnt: bl2: room for a larger BL33 on parallel NAND

BL2 loads the LZMA-compressed BL33 into EN7523_IMAGE_BUF (0x58000).  The
compressed image and the LZMA decoder's ~16 KiB of probabilities share
that buffer, so U-Boot has to stay under about 344 KiB packed.  With the
raw NAND stack the FiberHome HG5382A U-Boot is over that, and BL2 stops
with

  ERROR:   BL2: Failed to load image id 5 (-27)

(-EFBIG from load_image(), whose size check the pre-image-load hook
points at the decompression buffer).

For the parallel NAND BL2 only, widen the buffer to 0x80000.  It still
ends at 0x81900000, far below BL33_BASE, and nothing else is in use there
while BL2 runs.  SPI-NAND builds are unchanged, so their limit still
matches the BL2s already out in the field.

BL33_LIMIT is left alone: lzmaBuffToBuffDecompress() ignores the output
size it is given and unpacks whatever the LZMA header names, up to
5.5 MiB.  What bounds the unpacked U-Boot is U-Boot itself, whose early
stack sits at BL33_BASE + 2 MiB.
---
 plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h b/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
--- a/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
+++ b/plat/ecnt/en7523/include/platform_def.h
@@ -216,9 +216,18 @@
 #else
 #define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_OFFSET		(PLAT_ECNT_FIP_BASE + UL(0x80000))
 #endif
+#if defined(TCSUPPORT_PARALLEL_NAND)
+/*
+ * Holds the LZMA BL33 as read from the FIP plus the decoder's ~16 KiB of
+ * state; 0x58000 leaves no room for the parallel NAND U-Boot.  The buffer
+ * still ends far below BL33_BASE.
+ */
+#define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_SIZE		UL(0x80000)
+#else
 #define EN7523_IMAGE_BUF_SIZE		UL(0x58000)
 #endif
 #endif
+#endif
 
 #ifdef TCSUPPORT_BL2_OPTIMIZATION
 #ifdef IMAGE_BL21
-- 
2.43.0

